    "detailed_description": "<h1>Special Edition</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">This is a story of two magi, Vyn and Ilar, who find themselves trapped in a collapsing tower with their only hope for salvation being a difficult ritual. Or at least that is what Ilar tells you. The thing is - you don\u2019t remember anything, and Ilar\u2019s story makes less and less sense the closer you are to the ritual. Are they hiding things to protect you from the bitter truth, or are they deceiving you for some more nefarious reason?  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Guide Vyn\u2019s actions to death and beyond and uncover Ilar\u2019s truth. Are they your colleague, lover or something completely different? Read between the lines of what they are telling you, explore your surroundings for clues and use hands-on deduction to break the vicious circle and set them free. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">172 000 words or 8-40 hours of bittersweet suffering.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Over 500 choices, some more regrettable than others.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Around 50 false and 3 true endings. (It's not all bad, we promise)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A pretty nonbinary silver-tongued smug-face who might or might not murder you.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Yes, you do get to bone them, or get boned by them.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">But you don't have to if that's not your thing.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A magnificent cat who cares not if you live or die.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">An adorable eel friend.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Death. Lots of it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">An angry potato.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.poster.avif?t=1751837834\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.webm?t=1751837834\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.mp4?t=1751837834\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">This is a story of two magi, Vyn and Ilar, who find themselves trapped in a collapsing tower with their only hope for salvation being a difficult ritual. Or at least that is what Ilar tells you. The thing is - you don\u2019t remember anything, and Ilar\u2019s story makes less and less sense the closer you are to the ritual. Are they hiding things to protect you from the bitter truth, or are they deceiving you for some more nefarious reason?  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Guide Vyn\u2019s actions to death and beyond and uncover Ilar\u2019s truth. Are they your colleague, lover or something completely different? Read between the lines of what they are telling you, explore your surroundings for clues and use hands-on deduction to break the vicious circle and set them free. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">172 000 words or 8-40 hours of bittersweet suffering.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Over 500 choices, some more regrettable than others.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Around 50 false and 3 true endings. (It's not all bad, we promise)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A pretty nonbinary silver-tongued smug-face who might or might not murder you.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Yes, you do get to bone them, or get boned by them.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">But you don't have to if that's not your thing.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A magnificent cat who cares not if you live or die.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">An adorable eel friend.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Death. Lots of it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">An angry potato.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.poster.avif?t=1751837834\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.webm?t=1751837834\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1616280/extras/be64a808930ca1c4f15540336693b4b1.mp4?t=1751837834\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div></p>",
    "short_description": "Interactive story about two magi trying to survive a failed ritual. Learn from their deaths and untangle the mystery before you. Guide their actions as they come to terms with their past mistakes, and find forgiveness and love for each other.",
    "supported_languages": "English",
    "reviews": "\u201cSquare Weasel Studios has delivered an understated hit of an interactive visual novel, and I highly recommend it for people interested in that style of gaming experience.\u201d<br>9.5/10 \u2013 Chalgyr's Game Room<br><br>\u201cA gorgeously illustrated choose-your-own-adventure game that is filled with enigmatic characters and an alluring storyline that will have you just as wrapped in its mysteries as the protagonist is.\u201d<br>8/10 \u2013 Gaming Cypher<br><br>\u201cThe game\u2019s poignant storytelling experience stays with you once you reach its tender true ending. This VN is more than worth it, given the thoughtful messages and emotions it conveys.\u201d<br>GOTY \u2013 RPG Fan<br>",
